 "notes": [
  "Every figure here is the Chief Electoral Officer's as reported in the press. The state figures come from ETV Bharat's account of the press conference on the final roll on 21 September 2026, checked against The Hindu, and the district and constituency figures from the Hindustan Times and the Times of India in July 2026.",
  "The Chief Electoral Officer's website, which carries a constituency analysis of the draft roll, could not be reached, so no full table below the state was read.",
  "The roll before is the roll of 17 May 2026. The five reasons add exactly to the 20,12,557 names left off. Shifted, absent or other is 1,99,249 absent, 8,08,205 shifted and 14,441 other.",
  "The 44,777 names removed after the draft are 24,070 found ineligible at a hearing and 20,707 removed on Form 7 objections. ETV Bharat prints 20,708 for the second, one more than the other reports.",
  "The notices figure is ETV Bharat's, 12,98,779 unmapped electors and 45,37,547 with a logical discrepancy. The New Indian Express gives 45,37,613 for the second and 58,36,392 in all, 66 more.",
  "The Hindustan Times gives district percentages on the roll of 1 January 2025, which is not the roll the revision started from, so only its counts are used.",
  "The tables by district and constituency are the Chief Electoral Officer's own Formats 1B and 4B. Every constituency adds up to its district and every district to the state. The CEO has not published the names left off at the draft by district or constituency, so those tables run from the draft roll onward, and the fall from the January 2025 roll stands in for the rest.",
  "In Format 4B the additions and deletions by sex do not quite reconcile with the rolls by sex in most constituencies, by small amounts in both directions, which a change of recorded sex would explain. The tables here use the totals, which reconcile in every row. The three reasons it gives for deletions after the draft (death, shifting, a repeated entry) cover 28,229 of the 44,777."
 ],
 "cannot_show": [
  "The names left off in every district and every constituency. Only eleven districts and six constituencies were printed.",
  "The draft roll and the names left off by sex. The sources read give the roll before and the final roll by sex, and no source read gives the draft by sex.",
  "How many of the names added after the draft were people left off it and how many were enrolling for the first time."
 ]
